Hi HN, I&#x27;ve been building SaaS products for more than 20 years, and lately I&#x27;ve been thinking a lot about how we interact with software. When we add a feature, we have to figure out where it goes in the UI and how users will interact with it. Then users have to learn our particular way of doing something. AI lets us flip that around: the software can translate what the user wants into the actions needed to accomplish it. Yedric lets devs add a natural-language interface to an existing SaaS app. You expose your app&#x27;s actions and give it your docs and user context. Users can then ask for things like: • &quot;Export the table to a CSV&quot;
• &quot;Fix this disconnected integration&quot;
• &quot;Change my logo color to #B5E2F4&quot; We originally built Yedric for our own Shopif
